    {
      "id": "sec-4",
      "title": "Simple Harmonic Motion: A Special Periodic Motion",
      "module": "m42242",
      "est_minutes": 12,
      "locator": "CNXML module m42242",
      "objectives": [
        "Describe a simple harmonic oscillator.",
        "Explain the link between simple harmonic motion and waves."
      ],
      "misconceptions": [],
      "summary": [
        "Simple harmonic motion is oscillatory motion for a system that can be described only by Hooke’s law. Such a system is also called a simple harmonic oscillator.",
        "Maximum displacement is the amplitude X. The period T and frequency f of a simple harmonic oscillator are given by T=2πmk and f=12πkm, where m is the mass of the system.",
        "Displacement in simple harmonic motion as a function of time is given by x ( t ) = X cos 2π t T ."
      ],
